body:
The "select all" logic only selects items on the current page (`paginatedData`), but the check for whether all rows are selected compares `selectedRows.size === paginatedData.length`. This means:
1. If the user selects all on page 1, then navigates to page 2, the "select all" checkbox will appear checked even though page 2 items aren't selected.
2. The select all functionality doesn't work across pages.

Consider either: (a) clarifying this is per-page selection with a label like "Select all on this page", or (b) implementing true select-all that works across all pages in the dataset.
```suggestion
    // Determine if all rows on the current page are already selected
    const allSelectedOnPage = paginatedData.every(row => selectedRows.has(row.id));

    const newSelected = new Set(selectedRows);

    if (allSelectedOnPage) {
      // Deselect only the rows on the current page
      paginatedData.forEach(row => {
        newSelected.delete(row.id);
      });
    } else {
      // Select all rows on the current page, preserving selections from other pages
      paginatedData.forEach(row => {
        newSelected.add(row.id);
      });
    }

    setSelectedRows(newSelected);
    onChange?.(Array.from(newSelected));
```
